// One authored file holding a whole universe. Heading level sets the structure:
//   #    the universe itself (its identity)
//   ##   a chapter: Sides / Jobs / Narrative / Regions / ...
//   ###  an entry within a chapter (one side, one job type, one story beat)
//
// Each heading's data lives between `---` fences as `Label: value` fact lines, and the
// prose under the fence is what players read.
//
// Almost everything is optional. Reputation axes, standing tuning and the generation
// dials all fall back to engine defaults when you leave them out - which is why this file
// is short. Add chapters as you want them.

# [The Kestrel Verge](kestrel_verge)
---
Universe
Display: The Kestrel Verge
Station mix: 8%
Enemy mix: 12%
Nebula mix: 20%
Derelict chance: 60%
---
Past the last relay the charts are forty years old, and nobody has come to correct them.
Three colonies were planted out here. Two still answer.

## [Scenario](scenario)
---
Mode: story
---


// ---- The factions. Each heading key IS the side key. `Home` is a system coordinate on
// the galaxy grid; `Offers` names the job types this side hands out.
## [Sides](sides)

### [Hollin Compact](hollin)
---
Color: #44aa66
Character: settler
Disposition: neutral
Home: 0, 0
Values: honest 40, generous 30
Offers: patrol, escort, strike
Flies: Arvonian
---
The first colony, and the one that farms. They keep the relay running because nobody else will.

### [Deepwell Assembly](deepwell)
---
Color: #6688ff
Character: trader
Disposition: neutral
Home: 3, 1
Values: by-the-book 40, peaceful 20
Offers: survey, relay_run
Flies: 70% Ximni, 30% Arvonian
---
The second colony. Miners who sell what they dig and count every crate twice.

### [The Gleaners](gleaners)
---
Color: #cc5522
Character: pirate
Disposition: foe
Home: -3, -2
Values: fearsome 40, resourceful 30
Offers: salvage
Flies: Torgoth
---
They strip dead ships for a living, and they have stopped waiting for ships to die.


## [Captains](captains)

### [Edda Brake](edda)
---
Side: hollin
Title: the Relay Warden
Values: honest 40, kind 20
Roams: 0, 0
---
She has kept the lamp at Kestrel Relay for thirty years, and she remembers every ship that passed it.

### [Sable Orrin](sable)
---
Side: gleaners
Title: the Tallyman
Values: honest 40, by-the-book 30
Roams: -3, -2
---
The Gleaners' bookkeeper. She knows what every wreck in the Breakers fetched, and who was aboard when it stopped being a ship.


// ---- Job types the sides above can offer. The engine generates the individual jobs;
// these records say what KINDS exist and what they pay.
## [Jobs](jobs)

### [Patrol](patrol)
---
Tier: 2
Done when: destroy 3 enemies
Reward: 200 credits
---
Sweep a system and clear whatever is hunting in it.

### [Escort](escort)
---
Done when: reach 3, 1
Reward: 250 credits
---
See a freighter safely to its destination.

### [Salvage](salvage)
---
Done when: recover 2 tech
Reward: 150 credits, earns hollin selfish 20
---
Recover what is worth recovering, and do not ask where it came from.

### [Wreck Survey](survey)
---
Done when: scan 1 derelict
Reward: 220 credits
---
The Assembly wants every dead hull in the Verge on its books. Find one and scan it.

### [Relay Run](relay_run)
---
Done when: reach 0, 0
Fails when: 10 minutes
Reward: 180 credits
Penalty: 60 credits
---
Sealed tallies for Kestrel Relay. Carry them home and the Assembly pays on arrival.

### [Clear the Lanes](strike)
---
Tier: 3
Done when: destroy 6 enemies
Reward: 600 credits
---
The Compact does not ask this of strangers. Six hulls, and the lanes stay open a season.

